//! Font loading, SVG-path parsing, layout, and flattening.
//!
//! This module ports the subset of the Apache-2.0 `gmlewis/fonts`
//! package (plus `gmlewis/fonts/draw`) that the CAD text builder needs:
//!
//! * [`model`](crate::font::model) — `Font`, `Glyph`, 2D points, bounding
//!   boxes, and JSON decoding.
//! * [`svg`](crate::font::svg) — the absolute `M L C Q Z` path parser,
//!   `translate_path`, and `svg_num` formatting.
//! * [`layout`](crate::font::layout) — `Font::gen_path` and every `Alignment`.
//! * [`draw`](crate::font::draw) — `Anchor`, `Path`, `CompoundPath`,
//!   `Graphic`, and `to_graphic`.
//! * [`flatten`](crate::font::flatten) — true Bézier bounding boxes, polygon
//!   sampling, `to_profiles_tuples`, and `fit_to` / `scale_to_fit`.
//! * [`load`](crate::font::load) — gzip + JSON font loading with the
//!   reference search order.
//!
//! Only geometry is represented: fills and strokes are deliberately omitted
//! because the CAD layer consumes subpaths and their `clear` flags directly.

